  "id": "nominal-primitive-subtype-npm-ordinary-full-installed",
  "kind": "installed",
  "revision": "caff60b7f6acf60e06988f003b2823c0d2e0319e",
  "command": "ELAN_HOME='/app/.toolchains/elan' EMCC_CORES='1' EMSDK='/app/.toolchains/emsdk' LEAN_BRIDGE_LAKE_RUNTIME_ROOT='/app/build/lean-link-spike/lazy' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_MODES='full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_OUTPUT='/app/build/vo1469-npm-installed-ordinary-full-r1/selections' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_ROUTES='ordinary' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_PRIMITIVE_SUBTYPE_NPM_TEST='1' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' LEAN_WASM_EMSDK='/app/.toolchains/emsdk' LEAN_WASM_PROJECT_ROOT='/app' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' node '--max-old-space-size=3072' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' 'tests/helpers/nominal-primitive-subtype-npm-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce both complete npm archives. Offline installation follows author removal; unchanged JavaScript and strict TypeScript callers replay after moving the installed tree. The full API checks per-site constructors, normalization, repeated record fields, active variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards, rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Primitive-base nominal npm acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. The observed consumers are Node 22.23.2/Linux x64 and strict TypeScript with wasm32 values. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce from two authors, install offline after author removal and replay after physical relocation. Complete package archives, original records, selected sources and runtime inputs are retained; external toolchain binaries are not. The local compiler uses the repository's Nix command transport adapter, not a Nix sandbox. Other hosts need their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted acceptance of later revisions; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
