  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce both complete npm archives. Offline installation follows author removal; unchanged JavaScript and strict TypeScript callers replay after moving the installed tree. The standalone result-only API projects primitive payloads through scalars, copied containers, records, variants and aliases without any input constructor selections. Primitive-base nominal npm acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. The observed consumers are Node 22.23.2/Linux x64 and strict TypeScript with wasm32 values. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce from two authors, install offline after author removal and replay after physical relocation. Complete package archives, original records, selected sources and runtime inputs are retained; external toolchain binaries are not. The local compiler uses the repository's Nix command transport adapter, not a Nix sandbox. Other hosts need their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted acceptance of later revisions; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
